.claude/

# Personal agent instructions; not shared.
CLAUDE.md

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated caches (Rt bootstrapping is slow; results are reproducible)
Code/results/_cache/

# Sweep checkpoints. The horizon-1 checkpoints stay committed; a full sweep is
# 5 horizons x 12 experiments of weights that any run reproduces from scratch.
Code/checkpoints/horizon_*/

# Backtest and sweep output. A rolling backtest is 4 seasons x 3 horizons x
# every arm; at ~300 KB of predictions/metrics per run that is gigabytes, and
# any run reproduces it from the recorded seed and config. The aggregated
# _backtest/ tables are committed; the per-run trees are not.
Code/results/backtest_*/
Code/results/_backtest/*.csv
Code/checkpoints/backtest*/
Code/sweep/tasks.jsonl

# Raw SNVS respiratory-surveillance workbooks (Argentina Ministry of Health),
# ~61 MB together. Only Code/scrapers/build_amba_panel.py reads them; the loader
# uses the derived amba_*.csv files beside them, which ARE committed. Re-download
# from the national open-data portal to rebuild the panel.
Data/Buenos Aires Acute Respiratory Infections/informacion-publica-respiratorias-*.xlsx

# Columbus Public Health line-level extracts (one row per ED visit, hospitalisation
# or COVID case, with home ZIP). CPH cleared the data for public release at the
# aggregate level but asked that the line-level files stay with the project.
# Only Code/scrapers/build_columbus_panel.py reads them; the loader uses the
# committed weekly aggregates beside them (columbus_*_weekly_counts.csv).
Data/Columbus Influenza Data/ILI Specified Data-Franklin_final.xlsx
Data/Columbus Influenza Data/IAH Data CPH Franklin_final.csv
Data/Columbus Influenza Data/COVID Data CPH Franklin_final.csv

# Remove personal writings from class
Writings/
